Tenali Rama and the Cat’s Lesson (Raw Story)

One day, King Krishnadevaraya wanted to get rid of the rats in his kingdom.

He gave each courtier a cat and a cow, saying, “Take good care of the cat and feed it well with milk.”

All the courtiers happily fed their cats plenty of milk every day.

But Tenali Rama did something different.

He gave his cat very hot milk on the first day.

The cat burned its mouth and ran away.

After that, whenever Tenali offered milk, the cat refused to drink it.

Days later, the king came to check on the cats.

All the other cats were healthy and well-fed.

But Tenali’s cat looked thin and weak.

The king became angry and said, “Why did you not feed your cat properly?”

Tenali replied, “Your Majesty, I gave it milk every day, but it refuses to drink.”

To prove his point, Tenali brought a bowl of milk.

The cat ran away as soon as it saw it.

The king understood what had happened and smiled.

Tenali said, “Fear can be stronger than hunger.”

The king laughed and appreciated Tenali’s clever lesson.

💖 Moral:

Fear can change behavior more than force.
